cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TheoCP2K in your research, please cite the software and the underlying TheoDORE publication."
title: "TheoCP2K"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Merlo"
    given-names: "Mattia"
version: "0.1.3"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mattiamerlo-bot/TheoCP2K"
url: "https://github.com/mattiamerlo-bot/TheoCP2K"
abstract: >-
  TheoCP2K is a CP2K TDDFPT/NTO-cube extension of TheoDORE. It provides a
  graphical workflow for analysing CP2K output and NTO cube files, including
  hole/particle visualisation, fragment-based electron-hole analysis, and
  export of derived descriptors and figures.
keywords:
  - CP2K
  - TDDFPT
  - NTO
  - TheoDORE
  - excited states
  - electron-hole analysis
  - computational chemistry
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: "Plasser"
      given-names: "Felix"
  title: "TheoDORE: A toolbox for a detailed and automated analysis of electronic excited state computations"
  journal: "The Journal of Chemical Physics"
  year: 2020
  volume: 152
  issue: 8
  start: 084108
  doi: "10.1063/1.5143076"
